        "conclusion": "The patient presents with macrocephaly, dystonia, cerebral atrophy, subdural hemorrhage, glutaric aciduria, and aciduria. The most likely diagnosis based on this clinical picture is Glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency (GCDH), strongly supported by the presence of glutaric aciduria and other neurological features. Alternative considerations include Multiple acyl-CoA dehydrogenation deficiency (ETFA) and Glutaric acidemia type 3 (SUGCT).",
        "conclusionCode": [
